LinkedList:
i)A fundamental data structure in Computer Science.
ii)It is a linear data structure.
iii)Non-contuguous memory allocation.
iv)Efiicient insert/delete operations.


Collection of nodes.

node - [12,ref] [23,ref] [45,ref] [78,null]

head - points to the first node of the linkedlist
tail - points to the last node of the linkedlist

Types:
i)Singly LinkedList.
ii)Doubly LinkedList.

Node : three parts

pre : Points to the previous node.
data: Element of the node.
next:Points to the next node.

Can be moved forward/backward direction.

iii)Circular LinkedList.

last node point to the first node making it circular.

circular doubly linkedlist
next pointer of the last node points to the first node.
pre pointer of the first node points to the last node.

Finding middle node



